      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T10:59:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The old code sets the `SshSession.KEY` synchronously, the new one on this call back. There are a couple\nof places in the sshd package which perform `session.getAttribute(SshSession.KEY)` and assume it is not `null`.\nThis assumption was correct before this change but does it still hold? One such place is in the `DatabasePubKeyAuth` L112-113.\nAnother one is in the `CommandFactoryProvider`.\n\nWould it make sense to set the session eagerly (as before) and then *update* the peer address here when a better address\nis available?",
